the knowledge base us_statutes_26_32_c_2 includes:


% 26 U.S.C. 112 — us:statutes/26/112
the text of "26 USC 112(a), 112(b)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/112.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 112(a), 26 USC 112(b), 26 USC 112(c), 26 USC 112(d)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/112.yaml".

the hospitalization after combat zone termination limit years is 2, as stated in "26 USC 112(a), 112(b)".

rule amount_excluded_from_gross_income_by_reason_of_section_112 with provenance "26 USC 112(a), 26 USC 112(b), 26 USC 112(c), 26 USC 112(d)":
the amount excluded from gross income by reason of section 112 of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the tax unit is a tax_unit
    and the tax unit is member below grade of commissioned officer in armed forces
        and the tax unit is served in combat zone during month
        and the active service compensation as enlisted member excluding pensions and retirement pay of the tax unit is an amount M
        otherwise the tax unit is member below grade of commissioned officer in armed forces
        and the tax unit is hospitalized resulting from combat zone wounds disease or injury
        and the months beginning after combatant activities termination of the tax unit is a number K
        and the hospitalization after combat zone termination limit years is a number P
        and K <= P
        and it is not the case that the tax unit is vietnam combat zone hospitalization month after january 1978
        and the active service compensation as enlisted member excluding pensions and retirement pay of the tax unit is M
        otherwise M = 0
    and the tax unit is commissioned officer in armed forces excluding commissioned warrant officer
        and the tax unit is served in combat zone during month
        and the active service compensation as commissioned officer excluding pensions and retirement pay of the tax unit is an amount Q
        and the maximum enlisted amount for commissioned officer months of the tax unit is a number R
        and the minimum of Q and R is a number S
        otherwise the tax unit is commissioned officer in armed forces excluding commissioned warrant officer
        and the tax unit is hospitalized resulting from combat zone wounds disease or injury
        and the months beginning after combatant activities termination of the tax unit is a number T
        and the hospitalization after combat zone termination limit years is a number U
        and T <= U
        and it is not the case that the tax unit is vietnam combat zone hospitalization month after january 1978
        and the active service compensation as commissioned officer excluding pensions and retirement pay of the tax unit is Q
        and the maximum enlisted amount for commissioned officer months of the tax unit is R
        and the minimum of Q and R is S
        otherwise S = 0
    and the tax unit is armed forces member in missing status during vietnam conflict as result of conflict
        and it is not the case that the tax unit is officially absent from post of duty without authority
        and the armed forces missing status active service compensation of the tax unit is an amount V
        otherwise V = 0
    and the tax unit is civilian employee in missing status during vietnam conflict as result of conflict
        and the civilian employee missing status active service compensation of the tax unit is an amount W
        otherwise W = 0
    and N = M + S + V + W.


% 26 U.S.C. 32(c)(2) — us:statutes/26/32/c/2
the text of "26 USC 32(c)(2)(A), 26 USC 32(c)(2)(B)(i)-(v)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/32/c/2.yaml".

the text of "26 USC 32(c)(2)(A), 26 USC 32(c)(2)(B)(vi)" is at "sources/us/statutes/26/32/c/2.yaml".

rule earned_income_before_section_112_election with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(2)(A), 26 USC 32(c)(2)(B)(i)-(v)":
the earned income before section 112 election of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the employee compensation includible in gross income of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the net earnings from self employment after self employment tax deduction of the tax unit is an amount K
    and the pension or annuity amount of the tax unit is an amount P
    and the nonresident alien income not connected with united states business of the tax unit is an amount Q
    and the penal institution service compensation of the tax unit is an amount R
    and the subsidized state work activity service compensation of the tax unit is an amount S
    and a number T = M + K - P - Q - R - S
    and the maximum of 0 and T is N.

rule earned_income with provenance "26 USC 32(c)(2)(A), 26 USC 32(c)(2)(B)(vi)":
the earned income of a tax unit is an amount N if
    the earned income before section 112 election of the tax unit is an amount M
    and the taxpayer of the tax unit elects to treat section 112 excluded amounts as earned income
        and the amount excluded from gross income by reason of section 112 of the tax unit is an amount K
        otherwise K = 0
    and N = M + K.

